            <ArticleTitle>Substituted azaquinazolinones as modulators of GHSr-1a for the treatment of type II diabetes and obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2271-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2012.01.078</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Substituted azaquinazolinones were identified as antagonists of the GHSr-1A receptor for the treatment of type II diabetes and obesity. Optimisation for potency and LogD lead to the identification of orally bioavailable, potent antagonists with improved selectivity over hERG.</AbstractText>
